The cost of 3 baskets of green food is $3 \times G = 3 \times 25 = 75$.
The cost of 3 baskets of red food is $3 \times R = 3 \times 18 = 54$.
The total cost before the discount is $75 + 54 = 129$.
We get $2 off for each basket of red food. Since we bought 3 baskets of red food, the total discount is $3 \times 2 = 6$.
The total cost after the discount is $129 - 6 = 123$.

