55-5 = 50 That's how many cookies are left after Lani ate 5 cookies. Then we're going to divide these remaining 50 cookies into five jars. To find out how many cookies are in each jar, we will divide 50 by 5. 50 divided by 5 is 10. So, there were 10 cookies in each jar. \boxed{10}
Lani baked 55 cookies. She ate 5 cookies, so she had 55 - 5 = 50 cookies left. She put the rest of the cookies equally into five jars. So each jar contained 50 ÷ 5 = 10 cookies.
\boxed{10}
